   "slug": "speech-824715",
   "speaker": "Eric Abetz",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-20",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Asbestos Safety and Eradication Agency Bill 2013 was supported, establishing a national agency to coordinate asbestos safety and eradication, with Australia facing an estimated 13,000 mesothelioma cases by 2020 and 40,000 other asbestos-related cancers. The coalition criticised a $1.8 million funding cut from the originally pledged $12.3 million to $10.5 million, and urged broader state representation on the agency's council and expanded research functions."
